WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.648
Recent progress shows two useful ideas.

00:00:03.728 --> 00:00:07.376
First, learning across many tasks, rather than one
protein at a time,

00:00:07.456 --> 00:00:11.103
can help when labeled data is scarce.

00:00:11.183 --> 00:00:14.831
Second,

00:00:14.911 --> 00:00:18.559
foundation models trained on huge unlabeled
biological corpora capture structural and

00:00:18.639 --> 00:00:22.287
functional signal that raw sequences do not expose
directly.

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:26.014
Combining these ideas,

00:00:26.094 --> 00:00:29.742
a single model could learn general rules of
RNA-protein binding and apply them to interaction types it has never seen,

00:00:29.822 --> 00:00:33.470
which is exactly what a broad, sequence-only
predictor needs.
